        "fit": "cover",
        "shape": "rectangle",
        "hidden": false
      },
      {
        "padding": 0,
        "lineHeight": 1.5,
        "id": "markdown-8",
        "kind": "text",
        "name": "The Void is the NullDull blog: a place for the decisions,…",
        "text": "The Void is the NullDull blog: a place for the decisions, ideas and lessons behind what we build. It sits next to three other destinations, each with a different job:",
        "assetId": null,
        "frame": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 8,
          "width": 12,
          "height": 1
        },
        "frames": {},
        "color": "transparent",
        "background": "transparent",
        "fontSize": 18,
        "radius": 0,
        "align": "left",
        "fit": "cover",
        "shape": "rectangle",
        "hidden": false
      },
      {
        "padding": 0,
        "lineHeight": 1.5,
        "id": "markdown-9",
        "kind": "text",
        "name": "- **Support** explains how to do things in the product…",
        "text": "- **Support** explains how to do things in the product today, with the labels and commands you will actually see.\n- **What’s new?** records releases. Every entry is dated, and an entry only appears once the change is available.\n- **Roadmap** describes what we are working on and what comes next. A roadmap item is direction, not a promise or a release.",
        "assetId": null,
        "frame": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 9,
          "width": 12,
          "height": 1
        },
        "frames": {},
        "color": "transparent",
        "background": "transparent",
        "fontSize": 18,
        "radius": 0,
        "align": "left",
        "fit": "cover",
        "shape": "rectangle",
        "hidden": false
      },
      {
        "padding": 0,
        "lineHeight": 1.5,
        "id": "markdown-10",
        "kind": "text",
        "name": "These pages are themselves Grid pages. They are written as…",
        "text": "These pages are themselves Grid pages. They are written as drafts, saved, and then published explicitly by a Grid manager, the same way a customer would publish their own pages.",
        "assetId": null,
        "frame": {
          "x": 0,
          "y": 10,
          "width": 12,
          "height": 1
        },
        "frames": {},
        "color": "transparent",
        "background": "transparent",
